  "note": "Independent source rejudgment against RFC 7911 Section 2: \"However, the Path Identifier MUST be assigned in such a way that the BGP speaker is able to use the (Prefix, Path Identifier) to uniquely identify a path advertised to a neighbor.\" Read both tagged tests and all cited ownership/generator boundaries. Colliding received identifiers from two distinct sources for the same native prefix must leave under different local identifiers; replacement from the same source must retain its assigned identifier. These are falsifiable destination-visible pair assertions, not a demand that every local number differ from its received number. beginAdjOut still rejects retired/wrong-session/provenance writes, binds the current session's table and clears only replaced-session state; the moved code now also checks initial-write admission. Source keying, generatePath/mintLocked and bindSourcePath maintain local reservations, while recordNLRI and deletion preserve/release the proper owner. The tests cover uniqueness and stable replacement, not every recovery lifecycle race. Verdict enforced; the broadened producer admission does not undermine those assertions. No tests or discrimination replay ran.",
